{"entity":"story","version":1,"id":"ess-conformance-kernel","revision":1,"type":"aep.entity.create/v1","from_state":null,"to_state":"draft","changed":{"body":"## Context\n\n`systems/ekr/` is the contract the P1 crates implement. A specification nobody runs a suite\nagainst is prose. ESS synthesises the scenarios the kernel domain obliges — every command outcome,\nevery refusal, every lifecycle move — and holds a target to them; the report is what moves the\nspecification artifact to `conforming` in the planning store.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n`ess verify conform run --path systems/ekr` against the `ekr` conformance target reports every\nsynthesised scenario executed and none failed, and `aep plan artifact evidence\nexecutable-system-specification:ekr-v1 --from <report>` records it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `crates/ekr/src/conformance.rs` — the target: `ExecuteCommand` and `QueryView` over the kernel\n  library for `ekr.kernel.*` commands and views\n- `crates/ekr/tests/conformance.rs` — synthesises, runs, asserts zero failures\n- `systems/ekr/conformance/suite.json` — the synthesised suite, committed so drift is visible\n- `Taskfile.yml` — a `conform-check` task added to `check`\n\n## Notes\n\nDepends on `story:ekr-cli`. Skipped scenarios are counted and reported; a suite that skips is not\ngreen. The `ess-specify:coverage` skill is the reference for raising executed scenarios.\n","title":"ESS conformance suite over the kernel domain"},"args":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"## Context\n\n`systems/ekr/` is the contract the P1 crates implement. A specification nobody runs a suite\nagainst is prose. ESS synthesises the scenarios the kernel domain obliges — every command outcome,\nevery refusal, every lifecycle move — and holds a target to them; the report is what moves the\nspecification artifact to `conforming` in the planning store.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n`ess verify conform run --path systems/ekr` against the `ekr` conformance target reports every\nsynthesised scenario ex